  <Name>ERCOT Settlement Point Prices</Name>
  <DisplayName>ERCOT Settlement Point Prices</DisplayName>
  <Description>ERCOT real-time settlement point prices in dollars per MWh from system-wide-prices.json, polled every 15 minutes to match the interval ERCOT publishes. The endpoint carries the same 15 hubs and load zones as the real_time_spp.html page the 2021 Datadog dashboard scraped, one row per 15-minute interval of the operating day under rtSppData, so every path selects the newest row with the [-1:] slice. Prices include the Real-Time Reliability Deployment Price Adders, as the page states. Read against the live endpoint on 2026-09-17; see docs/guides/ercot-grid-dashboard.md. Thresholds are left nil because a sensible alert level is a market judgement; the 2021 winter event cleared at the $9,000 cap. The [-1:] slice that selects the newest row of a time-series array, and the [?(@.forecast==0)] filter that skips forecast rows, are JSONPath features this repository has not confirmed the platform's implementation accepts (docs/polling/api-poller-vendor-templates.md confirms a filter against response headers only). If those values read Unknown after assignment, the values themselves are wrong rather than the endpoint: assign scripts/sam-templates/ercot-system-conditions-html.apmtemplate instead, which reads the same numbers off ERCOT's HTML page with a script.</Description>
